WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.901
-Congratulations on anothe
season of "The Conners."

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-This is, of course,

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
a spinoff of "Roseanne,"
which you started --

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.206 size:84% position:42% line:92%
you did nine seasons on

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
beginning when you were
13 years old.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-That is --

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.477 line:92%
you were a very young person

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:12.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you grew up in front
of all of us.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was a very young,
awkward person.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.883
It's hard to have your teenage
years in front of everybody.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. In a weird way,
it's almost better

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.588 line:92%
to start when you're 7 than 13

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, that is --
-Right.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...a trippy time to get
in front of people.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because then they saw you cut
before it went weird.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right.
-Right?

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At 13, it's basically, like
take quick look

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's about to get
weird right today.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-And were you aware of that?

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, being that age,
could you even comprehend,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.639
"Oh, this is a very strang
place to be growing up"?

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:43.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not really, because my family
was in entertainment.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.846
So I think it was, for me,
it was weird not to do it.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:47.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-As soon as I started,

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Okay,
this feels correct."

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is where you're
supposed to be.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You're suppose to be on a set

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a 13-year-old.
-Yeah, which is weird, but -

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.155 line:92%
-But then -- and, of course,

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're also getting
an education.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does that mean
doing homework on set?

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that a big part of it?
-Yes.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was always jealous
because the older cast members

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
would get a break
when they didn't have a scene.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the kids would have to g
to the schoolroom

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sit in a little room
and do work, so --

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:14.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
But now my kids on the show,
it's so interesting,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.575 line:92%
because I'm used to, you know,

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, yeah,
it's time for school."

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
Their scene will end
and it's time for school,

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.147 line:92%
and I'm like, "Oh, bummer.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:24.951
And Ames, who plays my son
is like, "Oh, great. School.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:28.621
And I'm like, "What kind o
imposter child is this?"

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.724 line:92%
Like, "Who is this person?

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he's so brainy.
I mean, I look up to him.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.329 size:84% position:42%
-Do you reflect back
on yourself and wonder,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.231 line:92%
"Why wasn't I more into school?"

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Yeah, I see.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Just put it totally on him

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You -- I believe John Goodman

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
was here just yesterday
and he --

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.173 size:78% position:39%
you used to be called
Scruffy or Scuffy?

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:47.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Scuffy.
-Scuffy.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was the nickname
Scuffy for?

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So that was --
because I was a teenager,

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:59.119
I would kind of come in tire
with my shoes not fully on

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.020 size:88% position:44% line:92%
slowly scuffing the set.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Got you.
-So they would say,

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:05.191 size:88% position:44%
"Oh, here comes scuffy,"
because they'd hear me

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:06.459 size:75% position:38% line:92%
sort of scuffing in.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you were --
so just the teenager --

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...like, telltale stuff.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, happy.
-Yeah, you were happy.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it surreal walking bac
on the set

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.270 line:92%
after so many years away?

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.606 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It was crazy. The --

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:22.942
I was there for pre-production
so I was there while they were

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.210 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
putting up the set.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the first wall
of the utility room went up,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.816
which is like the back roo
that we didn't even shoot in

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
that much where
the washer and dryer are.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was just
one yellow wall.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I -- it blew me away
just seeing this

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:39.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
one tiny wall that
was a few feet.

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the whole set
of course went up.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I guess
it would be that --

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:46.432
it would be as if someone
just rebuilt your childhood home

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.634 line:92%
for you to go live in again,

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just watching it
slowly go up,

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
it must have been such a trip.
-Yeah.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then I've heard,
is it true that the couch

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:56.910
is not -- is the one thing
that is not the same couch

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not exactly
the same couch.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
We actually found
the original couch.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.750 line:92%
Some guy has, like, a TV museum.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
People think it's
in the Smithsonian.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:08.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was there for a brief time,
but it's no longer there.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:10.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then this guy stole it.
-This guy stole it.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.259
-He Nic Caged the "Roseanne"
couch from the Smithsonian

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's -- by the way, it's easy
to get a couch out, right?

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, exactly.
-To sneak out.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:20.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, so he has a bunch
of memorabilia.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:20.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had the couch.
And, for me,

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.469
it was really important to m
to get the original couch.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought that's, like --
-Yeah, it's --

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have to, right?
-Obviously, like,

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
the very fact that it was
in the Smithsonian

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
tells you this was...
-Sure.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.276 line:92%
-...an iconic piece of --

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But then in order
to get the couch,

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.413 line:92%
there were so many rules.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:37.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had to have thousands
of dollars of extra insuranc

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.152 size:78% position:39%
if we wanted to have
the couch on the set.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:41.654 size:81% position:41%
It could only be there
when we were shooting,

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
not on days where we were
just rehearsing.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:45.692
And then it had to be taken out.
It had to be cleaned.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:49.128
And it had to have its own
security guard, essentially.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah, and I was like,

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This couch is more
important than I am."

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.168 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Like, this is like --

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we thought that might b
too much.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.037 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-That might be too much.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I still was like, "Should we?
I don't know."

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think --
everything I know about actors

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
and their egos,
you don't want to have

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:07.313
a piece of furniture around that
people are being nicer to

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
than the actors.
-Right.

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-No, that's true.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.416 line:92%
-That would just spin them out

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But the other thing
that was funny to the cast

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.787 size:88% position:44%
we were like, "The couch
that we ate Cheetos on

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
and had our dirty feet on
is so" -- you know?

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Yeah, it's unbelievable.

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:20.960 line:92%
But, I guess, there you go

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.996
It's a piece of Americana
history at this point.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:24.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess so.
-You also --

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.098 line:92%
You created the show "The Talk."

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:28.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
You left recently to work on
some other things.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.970
When you leave a place like that
you've been for a long time,

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, obviously, I assume
you're very close

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the people
you work with there --

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you stay in touch
with everybody?

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:39.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I think they must b
thinking like,

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.280 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Please leave us alone."

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I left but I didn'
really leave.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm texting them,
"How did it go this week?

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.351
What is happening? Who's there?"
-Yeah.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.387
-That's all right. When I left
"SNL," I did the same thing.

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:49.956
I was so -- I still wanted to be
super invested in that place

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.358
And then I realized they were --
they basically had to

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
eventually tell me --
-They move on.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.395
-Yeah, and they're also like
"You know we're working, right

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:58.665
This is a workplace and we don't
need to tell you all day, like

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
how work is."
-Yeah.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, congratulations
on the show.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.637
It is so lovely having you here.
-Thank you.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And looking forward to a ne
season of "The Conners."

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give it up for Sara Gilbert,
everybody.

